  "numerical_failure": {
    "category": "correctness",
    "affected_api": "sympy.core.sympify._convert_numpy_types",
    "observed_behavior": "Calling sympy.Float on a NumPy float32 infinity causes _convert_numpy_types (via sympify) to call a.as_integer_ratio(), raising OverflowError: \"cannot convert Infinity to integer ratio\".",
    "expected_behavior": "Instead of converting infinity via as_integer_ratio(), _convert_numpy_types should detect positive/negative infinity and return sympy.Float('inf') or sympy.Float('-inf') respectively.",
    "manifestation": "exception",
    "trigger_conditions": [
      "Input to sympy.Float (via sympify/_convert_numpy_types) is a NumPy float value representing positive infinity, e.g. numpy.float32(float('inf'))."
    ],
    "input_output_examples": [
      {
        "input": "sympy.Float(np.float32(float('inf')))",
        "buggy_output": "OverflowError: cannot convert Infinity to integer ratio",
        "expected_output": "sympy.Float('inf')",
        "value_kind": "exception",
        "source": "issue#27284 reproducer and traceback; fix in sympy/core/sympify.py _convert_numpy_types"
      }
    ],
    "oracle_clues": [
      "The traceback shows _convert_numpy_types calling `p, q = a.as_integer_ratio()` and raising OverflowError when the input is infinity.",
      "The diff for sympy/core/sympify.py adds checks `if np.isposinf(a): return Float('inf')` and `elif np.isneginf(a): return Float('-inf')` before calling `a.as_integer_ratio()`."
    ]
  },
  "numerical_characteristics": {
    "dtype": null,
    "precision": null,
    "magnitude": null,
    "tolerance": null,
    "category_specific_evidence": [
      "sympify on infinite numpy float inputs violated the requirement that the input can be converted to a rational via `a.as_integer_ratio()`; previously this raised `OverflowError: cannot convert Infinity to integer ratio` for infinity values.",
      "Concrete failing values: `sympify(np.float32(float('inf')))` raised `OverflowError: cannot convert Infinity to integer ratio` (before fix).",
      "Concrete passing/expected results after fix: `Float(numpy.float32(float('inf'))) == S.Infinity` and `Float(numpy.float32(float('-inf'))) == S.NegativeInfinity`.",
      "Fix logic indicates the necessary numerical property: detect positive/negative infinity before attempting ratio conversion (`if np.isposinf(a): return Float('inf')` and `elif np.isneginf(a): return Float('-inf')`)."
    ],
    "reproduction_risks": [
      "Reproduction requires NumPy to be installed (`if not numpy: skip(\"numpy not installed.\")`)."
    ]
  },
